VLS(1)                        ZOAU Command Syntax                       VLS(1)

NAME

	vls - Lists VSAM datasets, alternate indexes, and paths that match a
	pattern.

SYNOPSIS

	vls [-dhlmv] <DATASET-PATTERN>

	-d
		Print out debug messages.

	-h
		Display syntax help.

	-l
		List details.

	-m
		List migrated datasets.

	-v
		Print verbose information.

DESCRIPTION

	vls lists VSAM datasets that match the pattern which is specified to stdout.
	The VSAM components are included for each VSAM cluster.

	If you specify -m, migrated datasets will also be displayed in the output.

DATASET PATTERNS

	The following rules apply to <DATASET-PATTERN>.

	The high-level-qualifier (HLQ) must be specified in full.
	An asterisk (*) matches any sequence of characters.
	A question mark (?) matches a single character.

EXAMPLES

	List all VSAM datasets that start with IBMUSER.MVSCMD

		vls IBMUSER.MVSCMD.*

EXIT VALUES

	0
		At least one dataset was found matching a dataset-pattern

  	1
		No datasets were found.

	other
		Error in dataset listing. See error messages for details.

